WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:03.395
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:07.380
NARRATOR: The first
modern steam engine

00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:10.230
was invented in England
in the early 1700s,

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:12.750
helping launch the
Industrial Revolution.

00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:15.750
Today, there's a
return to steam power.

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:18.240
Due to its different
configuration and combustion

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:21.300
process, a steam engine
produces less pollution

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:23.325
than a regular internal
combustion engine.

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:30.840
This steam engine burns fuel in
an external combustion chamber.

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:34.250
The resulting heat turns water
into pressurized steam that

00:00:34.250 --> 00:00:36.770
enters the cylinders,
pushing pistons,

00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:39.305
turning a crank shaft that
powers the drive train.

00:00:40.610 --> 00:00:43.580
Because this engine doesn't
burn fuel inside the cylinders

00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:45.710
like a traditional
car engine, it

00:00:45.710 --> 00:00:49.700
can run on any type or mixture
of fuels with fewer emissions.

00:00:51.560 --> 00:00:54.710
The circular engine block
is made of aluminum.

00:00:54.710 --> 00:00:56.690
Technicians install
studs to hold

00:00:56.690 --> 00:00:59.600
six stainless steel cylinders.

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:02.030
Due to the constant
exposure to steam,

00:01:02.030 --> 00:01:04.749
all engine parts are made
of rust proof materials.

00:01:06.530 --> 00:01:09.690
The technicians insert a
piston into each cylinder.

00:01:09.690 --> 00:01:11.810
The piston is
aluminum with a heat

00:01:11.810 --> 00:01:14.690
resistant carbocation
and glider to isolate

00:01:14.690 --> 00:01:17.000
it from the cylinder wall.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:19.340
They connect the piston
rods to the crankshaft

00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:22.040
in the center with the
specially designed component

00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:23.690
called a spider bearing.

00:01:23.690 --> 00:01:27.260
This bearing is designed to
modify the piston stroke,

00:01:27.260 --> 00:01:30.950
producing a smoother rotation
of the crankshaft and more power

00:01:30.950 --> 00:01:32.570
to the engine.

00:01:32.570 --> 00:01:35.690
Unlike a traditional car
engine with cylinders arranged

00:01:35.690 --> 00:01:39.410
in line, these cylinders are
in a radio configuration,

00:01:39.410 --> 00:01:42.110
and therefore equidistant
from the center.

00:01:42.110 --> 00:01:44.090
This prevents the
engine from warping

00:01:44.090 --> 00:01:46.610
under high temperatures.

00:01:46.610 --> 00:01:48.800
They place a counterbalance
over their spider

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:52.160
bearing to further smooth
the motion of the crankshaft.

00:01:52.160 --> 00:01:55.700
Now, they install a
pushrod over each cylinder.

00:01:55.700 --> 00:01:58.850
It operates a valve, which
let steam enter the cylinder

00:01:58.850 --> 00:01:59.735
and move the piston.

00:02:01.160 --> 00:02:04.220
They insert the base of each
pushrod into a guide ring.

00:02:07.340 --> 00:02:09.860
Then attach the cylinder
heads, each of which

00:02:09.860 --> 00:02:12.110
houses a steam entry valve.

00:02:12.110 --> 00:02:14.195
They insert the
pushrod into the valve.

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:21.440
Then to complete
the engine assembly,

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:23.990
they install the cam,
which pushes the push

00:02:23.990 --> 00:02:25.805
rods as the shaft spins.

00:02:27.470 --> 00:02:29.360
The factory hooks
up every completed

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:31.745
engine for a couple of rounds
of performance testing.

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:36.920
First to trial run using air
pressure to check for leaks

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:40.550
and to verify that all
components operate correctly.

00:02:40.550 --> 00:02:43.550
If everything's fine, then
they repeat the process

00:02:43.550 --> 00:02:44.390
with steam pressure.

00:02:47.190 --> 00:02:50.580
This type of steam engine can
power many types of machines

00:02:50.580 --> 00:02:54.420
from cars, trucks, and
boats to electric generators

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:56.010
as we see here.

00:02:56.010 --> 00:02:58.770
In a vehicle, it doesn't
require a transmission

00:02:58.770 --> 00:03:01.215
because it produces so
much rotational power.

00:03:03.350 --> 00:03:05.180
Now, for the heat exchanger.

00:03:05.180 --> 00:03:08.315
The component which turns water
into engine powering steam.

00:03:09.740 --> 00:03:11.720
Technicians use
a motorized wheel

00:03:11.720 --> 00:03:14.660
to wind 20 feet of stainless
steel tubing into a coil.

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:20.680
They bind the coil
with steel thread,

00:03:20.680 --> 00:03:23.905
putting a stitch in between each
tube to create a minute gap.

00:03:25.480 --> 00:03:28.670
That way, when fuel burns
in the combustion chamber,

00:03:28.670 --> 00:03:31.660
the heat can travel over
at in between the tubes,

00:03:31.660 --> 00:03:34.930
heating the water inside faster
and more efficiently than

00:03:34.930 --> 00:03:37.330
if the heat would contact
only the coils top

00:03:37.330 --> 00:03:38.260
and bottom surfaces.

00:03:39.790 --> 00:03:43.090
The result, superheated
steam in just 5 seconds.

00:03:43.090 --> 00:03:45.965
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:03:50.440 --> 00:03:52.840
They stack six of
these coils, one

00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:55.150
to feed steam to each cylinder.

00:03:55.150 --> 00:03:57.190
This nest of tubes
form the engine's

00:03:57.190 --> 00:03:58.810
primary heat exchanger.

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:05.650
They test it using any number
of fuels even waste fuels, which

00:04:05.650 --> 00:04:08.230
would otherwise be
discarded, such as used motor

00:04:08.230 --> 00:04:11.230
oil and used vegetable oil
from restaurant fryers.

00:04:12.490 --> 00:04:14.890
Virtually anything that
burns will do the job.

00:04:16.630 --> 00:04:19.870
The fuel combusts at low
pressure, not at high pressure

00:04:19.870 --> 00:04:22.120
as in a gas or diesel engine.

00:04:22.120 --> 00:04:25.300
That means burning fossil
fuels to make steam produces

00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:28.390
far fewer greenhouse
gases and most

00:04:28.390 --> 00:04:31.330
hydrocarbons burn off
completely within the sealed

00:04:31.330 --> 00:04:33.190
combustion chamber.

00:04:33.190 --> 00:04:36.130
You never have to refill
or top off the water,

00:04:36.130 --> 00:04:39.350
because a condenser cools
the steam back into water,

00:04:39.350 --> 00:04:41.830
which then circulates.

00:04:41.830 --> 00:04:44.150
Water is not only
the working fluid,

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:46.750
it also acts as the
engine lubricant,

00:04:46.750 --> 00:04:49.270
so the steam engine
doesn't require motor oil.

00:04:52.140 --> 00:04:55.110
Besides fuel combustion,
this modern steam engine

00:04:55.110 --> 00:04:58.260
can run off other heat
sources, such as solar heat

00:04:58.260 --> 00:05:00.510
and exhaust heat from
furnaces or engines.

00:05:00.510 --> 00:05:03.860
[MUSIC PLAYING]

